# Very short description of the package


## Installation

Add VCS repositories on composer.json

```
"repositories": [
	{
		"type": "vcs",
		"url": "git@github.com:atrioteam/laravel-deployment.git"
	}
],
```

You can install the package via composer:

```bash
composer require atrioteam/laravel-deployment
```

## Usage

### Deployment via http

Run the command `deployment:setup` with argument `http` (command will ask for input if not provided).

- add env variable DEPLOY_AUTH_KEY (env file must be present on destination host from the very first action run)

- configure secrets on github
    - FTP_HOST
    - FTP_USER
    - FTP_PASSWORD
    - DOMAIN_NAME
    - DEPLOY_AUTH_KEY (same as env variable)
    - GH_AUTH_TOKEN : a valid auth github token to access private repositories (if any)

### Deployment via ssh

Run the command `deployment:setup` with argument `ssh` (command will ask for input if not provided).

Follow instructions here: https://github.com/atrioteam/Helper/blob/master/deployment_hostinger/README.md#deployment-su-vps-hostinger

### Testing

```bash
php artisan test ./vendor/atrioteam/laravel-deployment
```

### Changelog

Please see [CHANGELOG](CHANGELOG.md) for more information what has changed recently.

## Contributing

Please see [CONTRIBUTING](CONTRIBUTING.md) for details.

### Security

If you discover any security related issues, please email dev@atrio.it instead of using the issue tracker.

## Credits

